<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4197" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Astŭra</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄστυρα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river in Asturia</i>, now <i>Esla</i>, <i><span class="en">Flor. 4, 12,
			54</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river</i> (and f., <i>an
				island and town</i>) <i>in Latium</i>, <i>near which Cicero had a villa</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				12, 40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 6, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
			13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 9, § 57</span></i>; cf. Mann.
			Ital. I. p. 620.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>